From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:17:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 092/112] HPF: the HP ladder's resonance and its level
 normalisation to full resolution

1.2.1 cut the HPF's resonance to 256 steps (FilterSet::setConfig(), against the rustle of per-block jumps, which the
per-sample coefficient ramps now avoid) and normalised the output with 2^31 / (resonance >> 23), 1 / resonance to 8
bits: a modulated or automated HPF resonance moved the level in steps of up to 0.77 dB (spec point 14). Now the
resonance keeps its resolution and the normalisation is 2^31 / (x - k / x), x = resonance / 2^23, in double: k keeps
the level at the minimum resonance (every HPF at resonance 0 or 1, 1.2.1's 1 / 8) exactly and falls away above, where
1.2.1's steps are small: within 0.14 dB of 1.2.1 at every knob value 0..50, within half its own step in between.
tests/filters filter_neutral hpres (level at 500 Hz, 360 resonances 0..45, step against the neighbours' slope):
v17 0.82 dB, now 0.085 (the bend where the resonance leaves its minimum).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
---
 src/deluge/dsp/filter/filter_set.cpp |  6 ++++--
 src/deluge/dsp/filter/hpladder.cpp   | 11 ++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/deluge/dsp/filter/filter_set.cpp b/src/deluge/dsp/filter/filter_set.cpp
index e0b2e526..4bf4a9e7 100644
--- a/src/deluge/dsp/filter/filter_set.cpp
+++ b/src/deluge/dsp/filter/filter_set.cpp
@@ -349,8 +349,10 @@ int32_t FilterSet::setConfig(q31_t lpfFrequency, q31_t lpfResonance, FilterMode
 	lpfMode_ = lpfmode;
 	hpfMode_ = hpfmode;
 	routing_ = routing;
-	// Insanely, having changes happen in the small bytes too often causes rustling
-	hpfResonance = (hpfResonance >> 21) << 21;
+	// 1.2.1 cut the HPF's resonance to 256 steps here ("having changes happen in the small bytes too often causes
+	// rustling": each block's change jumped). mastertune v18: the coefficients move per sample from block to block, so
+	// the resonance keeps its full resolution: a modulated or automated one no longer moves in steps of up to 0.8 dB
+	// (tests/filters filter_neutral hpres)
 
 	if (LPFOn) {
 		if ((lpfMode_ == FilterMode::SVF_BAND) || (lpfMode_ == FilterMode::SVF_NOTCH)) {
diff --git a/src/deluge/dsp/filter/hpladder.cpp b/src/deluge/dsp/filter/hpladder.cpp
index 511f3653..509b6b38 100644
--- a/src/deluge/dsp/filter/hpladder.cpp
+++ b/src/deluge/dsp/filter/hpladder.cpp
@@ -41,7 +41,16 @@ q31_t HpLadderFilter::setConfig(q31_t hpfFrequency, q31_t hpfResonance, FilterMo
 	// Extra feedback
 	hpfProcessedResonance = multiply_32x32_rshift32(hpfProcessedResonance, extraFeedback) << 1;
 
-	hpfDivideByProcessedResonance = (q31_t)(2147483648.0 / (double)(hpfProcessedResonance >> (23)));
+	// The output's normalisation, 1 / resonance. 1.2.1 divided by hpfProcessedResonance >> 23, an integer from 8 to
+	// 143: 1 / resonance to 8 bits, in steps of up to 0.8 dB as the resonance moves (a modulated or automated one steps
+	// audibly). mastertune v18: to full resolution, 2^31 / (x - k / x), x = hpfProcessedResonance / 2^23. k keeps the
+	// level at the minimum resonance (x 8.94, 1.2.1's 1 / 8: every HPF with its resonance at 0 or 1) exactly as it was,
+	// and falls away as the resonance goes up, where the steps are small: within 0.14 dB of 1.2.1's at every value
+	// the knob sets (0 to 50), within half of 1.2.1's own step in between
+	constexpr double kMinX = 75000000.0 / 8388608.0; // the minimum resonance's x (134217728 * extraFeedback)
+	constexpr double kK = (kMinX - 8.0) * kMinX;
+	const double x = (double)hpfProcessedResonance / 8388608.0;
+	hpfDivideByProcessedResonance = (q31_t)std::lround(2147483648.0 / (x - kK / x));
 
 	// 1 = 536870912
 	int32_t moveabilityTimesProcessedResonance = multiply_32x32_rshift32(hpfProcessedResonanceUnaltered, fc);
-- 
